  "body": "### Summary\n\nAs a reader, I want a search button directly in the bottom bar, so that I can search without going through \"Plus\". (Operator feedback on the latest iPhone build, 2026-11-14.)\n\n### Today\n\nThe floating Liquid Glass tab bar has four items: Catégories, Favoris, Messages, Plus (LOT-170, #296, the legacy navigation). Search is reached through \"Plus\".\n\n### Ask\n\n- Add a **fifth item, Recherche**, placed left of \"Plus\" (…), for quick access.\n- Reference: WhatsApp shows 5 items on one bar. It does not feel cramped and wastes no space. Keep that balance on the smallest iPhone width and in landscape.\n\n### Scope and notes\n\n- **M4** (operator, 2026-11-14), filed as beta feedback. It differs from the legacy bar (four items) on purpose, as #869 did.\n- The search screen itself is unchanged; only its entry point moves. \"Plus\" keeps its search entry, or drops it if it becomes redundant (decide in the PR, with the operator).\n- Check the iPad and Duo/foldable layouts: if the sidebar replaces the tab bar there, add the same entry to the sidebar.\n- Check #649 (page controls under the tab bar in landscape) and the pager placement (#565) with a wider bar.\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] The tab bar shows 5 items on iPhone, with Recherche left of Plus; the labels fit at the default and the largest supported Dynamic Type size, or the bar follows the system's compact rule.\n- [ ] Tapping Recherche opens the existing search screen; the tab state survives rotation (#559).\n- [ ] Screenshots on the smallest and the largest iPhone, and in landscape, are in the PR.\n- [ ] The GAP row for the root navigation is updated through the PR's `### Ledger` section (deliberate difference).\n\n### Decision (operator, 2026-11-14)\n\nThe 5-item bar becomes the **experimental option « Recherche dans la barre »** (`ExperimentalFeature.searchTab`, #903). The default stays the legacy 4-item bar (ezzz's point). The code goes to `App/SwiftHFR/Experimental/SearchTab/`, marked `// EXPERIMENTAL(searchTab, #896)`. M5, claimed by the operator, `experimental`.\n\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
